    {
      "id": 357284,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A previously disclosed vulnerability (CVE-2023-30584) was patched insufficiently in commit 205f1e6. The new path traversal vulnerability arises because the implementation does not protect itself against the application overwriting built-in utility functions with user-defined implementations.\n\nPlease note that at the time this CVE is issued, the permission model is an experimental feature of Node.js.",
